@@ -0,0 +1,295 @@
+# Codex automatic approval plugin bridge
+
+The local desktop installation is 3.14.4. This patch is based on source commit
+29628c9acdb81b703bbd4080c207a0e7ce5e276e (3.14.3). The independent desktop
+distribution retains the installed Electron executable and native assets, and
+replaces the Agent and desktop JavaScript with source-built bundles. This mixed patch-level compatibility must be
+tested and identified in the artifact metadata.
+
+## Ownership and flow
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+  participant R as Session runtime
+  participant H as Configured permission hook
+  participant P as Plugin process
+  participant M as Native model adapter
+  R->>H: PermissionRequest with exact tool input
+  H->>R: Obtain approval lease and authoritative context
+  H->>P: stdin + event-scoped bridge socket/token
+  P->>H: context/read
+  P->>H: model/complete with reviewer messages and read tool schemas
+  H->>M: Host-bound review model, credentials remain in host
+  M-->>P: Normalized text/tool calls
+  P-->>H: allow / deny / ask + assessment
+  H->>R: Validate lease, update per-turn denial state
+  R->>R: Execute once, return denial feedback, or prompt human
+```
+
+The runtime owns authoritative human input, session rejection action history, and per-turn counters.
+The configured hook owns its transient lease; the execution adapter owns socket
+I/O. A bridge exists only for the enabled `codex-auto-approval` plugin's foreground
+PermissionRequest process. The host resolves the configured review model; the plugin
+cannot choose it through request parameters or retrieve credentials. No shell or
+execution capability is exposed. Standard permission checking runs
+before and after hooks; hard denies and plan restrictions retain precedence.
+
+## Contract
+
+Bridge version 2 uses bounded NDJSON requests `{ id, token, method, params }` and
+responses `{ id, result }` or `{ id, error: { code, message, retryable,
+businessCode?, httpStatus?, requestId?, retryAfterMs? } }`.
+`context/read` returns binding, complete action, main and actual review selections, trusted
+human input records, limited visible evidence, previous denials, and deadline.
+`model/complete` accepts reviewer messages and the fixed `read_file/list_files`
+schemas and returns the existing Reviewer completion shape. Native model
+credentials are not returned. Every request is checked against the active lease.
+
+`ZCODE_APPROVAL_BRIDGE_SOCKET` and `ZCODE_APPROVAL_BRIDGE_TOKEN` are ephemeral
+child-process environment overlays. They are minted by the adapter, never
+accepted from inherited environment or project configuration, and never persisted
+or sent to the model. Windows uses named pipes; other platforms use private Unix
+sockets. `ZCODE_APPROVAL_BRIDGE_VERSION=2` advertises this contract. Missing bridge,
+invalid input, missing authoritative context, and transport failures request
+human approval, never allow.
+
+PermissionRequest gains `behavior: ask` and optional `assessment` and `bindingId`
+fields. Ask dominates automatic allow; deny dominates ask. A deny with
+`interrupt: true` stops the turn after delivering the denial tool result.
+Only a validated Codex plugin result contributes to per-turn counters.
+
+Cancellation ends the lease and native model request. Model selection, workspace,
+branch or human authorization changes invalidate the result. Stale results ask
+for a new review. An allow grants only the current unchanged tool call and never
+updates permission rules. On turn change denial counters reset; rejected actions remain in history. Policy
+denials trip at 3 consecutive or 10 among the last 50 reviews; technical errors
+are not policy denials. Plugin toggles take effect in new sessions.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+The assessment schema is shared in the contracts hook module. Permission error
+assembly owns the optional breaker turn-control result, so the permission flow
+does not duplicate error envelopes or exceed the existing module size boundary.
+
+The approval sidecar uses `ModelRetryBudget.SingleAttempt` for each native completion.
+The shared reviewer owns the outer three-attempt budget, including snapshot restarts;
+the adapter also counts initial attempts by request id. This prevents the native default
+eleven-attempt retry policy from multiplying the approval budget. Native authentication
+and runtime header refresh remain in the host.
+
+The reviewer supplies an explicit per-request output budget: at most 8192 tokens,
+clamped to the current native model's advertised maximum. Native ModelFactory
+deliberately binds only the selected reasoning level; omitting an output budget
+fails before transport. Review must preserve that bound reasoning level. Tests
+use the real native Model request validator, not only a permissive model mock.
+
+Cover real hook subprocess allow/deny/ask/cancel, malformed responses, wrong-token
+and stale leases, parallel sessions, model switching with inherited options,
+read-only investigation, policy feedback, turn-scoped breaker, hard permission
+rules, offline artifact installation, disable/uninstall and desktop startup.
+Keep the original independent CLI and its 52 tests compatible. Record actual
+checks and unverified remote-workspace support without claiming complete Codex
+equivalence. No database migration, public publication or global auth change.
+
+## CodexAutoApproval permission entry
+
+The local Windows permission menu adds a fourth radio option named exactly
+`CodexAutoApproval`; the marketplace listing has the same display name. The
+stable lowercase technical plugin id remains
+`codex-auto-approval@codex-auto-review-local` for upgrade compatibility.
+No new Agent permission enum or unimplemented `auto` mode is introduced.
+The regular Chinese subtitle is exactly `由Codex迁移的自动审批`.
+The existing new-session-required message takes precedence while enabling is blocked.
+
+The native plugin configuration owns enabled state. The existing plugin service
+and plugin management store own mutations and projection; the composer owns
+only its native permission draft. Selecting CodexAutoApproval first enables the
+plugin at workspace scope, waits for the successful native RPC/list refresh,
+then selects native `build`. Selecting any native permission first disables the
+plugin at workspace scope, then changes the native permission draft. Plan is an
+independent constraint and does not toggle the plugin. A previously enabled
+plugin aligns the idle composer with build. Workspace overrides take precedence
+over the user default; other workspaces retain their own effective settings.
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+  participant U as Permission menu
+  participant S as Plugin management store
+  participant H as Native plugin service/config
+  participant C as Composer draft owner
+  U->>S: Select option, workspace-scoped enabled command
+  S->>H: plugins/setEnabled
+  H-->>S: Persisted plugin result + refreshed effective listing
+  S-->>U: Success for the same workspace context
+  U->>C: build or selected native permission
+```
+
+Switching is locked while a workspace task is running or a toggle is pending.
+On RPC failure the existing store restores the projection, displays the error,
+and no native permission change is admitted. A stale workspace response cannot
+change the new workspace draft. Opening the menu refreshes the effective plugin
+state. The entry is hidden for non-Windows, browser and remote workspaces, and
+when this plugin is not installed. Keyboard cycling follows the same command
+path. Installed/enabled at user scope remains a default for new sessions;
+plugin enable is admitted only from a new-session composer. An existing session
+that has no enabled plugin cannot hot-load its frozen Hook catalog; its option
+is disabled with a new-session explanation. Disable remains available for idle
+existing sessions, and the activity bridge cancels/restores native approval.
+The bridge activity check merges user then project enable flags with the same
+last-defined precedence as native config; workspace enable can override user
+disable and must not be rejected by an independent any-false check.
+
+Desktop acceptance must verify four distinct radio entries, exact display name
+in the plugin settings, keyboard enable, native-mode disable with persisted
+workspace config, Plan independence, restored automatic review, original denial
+and failure behavior, and uninstall restoring native approval. Repack only an
+independent desktop copy; preserve the original installation and active app.
+
+The adapted production desktop uses `ZCode AutoReview` as its default runtime
+application identity. This preserves the existing adapted userData directory,
+avoids the official app's single-instance lock, and makes `ZCode.exe` directly
+launchable without a cmd environment wrapper. Development and Preview defaults,
+explicit test overrides and shared native user plugin settings stay unchanged.
+
+## 0.1.2 review-first lifecycle
+
+Only a loaded foreground CodexAutoApproval PermissionRequest process advertises
+review-first capability. Runtime tool permission flow owns the lifecycle keyed by
+requestId/toolCallId/turnId. Other permission hooks retain their responder race.
+Native hard denies and Plan constraints are checked before review. The native
+interaction registry owns each manual answer; projections never own decisions.
+
+Order: permission_review_started -> review hook -> permission_review_completed.
+Allow executes once without permission_requested; deny returns corrective feedback
+without execution or manual prompt. On technical failure the broker registers
+its answer receiver, then its onRegistered callback emits permission_requested
+with reviewFailure {code,message}, then starts the legacy client request.
+First and duplicate clicks share the existing one-shot registry. Cancellation
+closes the lease and clears projected progress; stale model, authorization,
+workspace, branch, or plugin state cannot authorize execution. At most three
+review attempts share one 90-second deadline. Persistent changes fall back.
+
+The host passes an immutable full TraceContext plus bound session/turn/query/tool
+identity into owner.complete. The stream runs inside explicit native invocation
+context with querySource=auto_review and truthful auxiliary session type=other;
+only the native adapter builds authentication and attribution headers. It uses
+streamText, collects text_delta and final tool_call events, keeps hidden
+reasoning only in private continuation state, rejects errors, truncated output and a missing finish. Selected
+provider/model/reasoning and min(8192, model maximum) output budget are preserved.
+
+Review events are durable session facts. Desktop and replay derive a reviewing
+label on the existing tool row, without creating a pending human interaction.
+Failure reasons cross contracts, bridge, v3 and v4 as bounded sanitized code/message.
+No credentials, raw provider bodies, or stack traces enter the permission dialog.
+The dialog says “自动审查失败，需人工确认” and exposes the sanitized cause.
+
+Local release is 0.1.2 under a new artifact directory; the installed desktop and
+user credentials are not replaced. Acceptance records include core/host checks,
+baseline-only failures, isolated Windows UI screenshots, SHA256 checksums, and
+a real current GLM review. Local stub success cannot prove server interception
+is fixed; record live failure and manual fallback if the real service rejects it.
+
+Admission also checks current native plugin activity through ApprovalBridgePort.isActive. A frozen loaded hook catalog after disable must not create another review-progress phase; an in-flight disable still cancels its existing lease and falls back.
+
+## 0.1.3 independent review model (normative current contract)
+
+### Configuration owner and interface
+
+The native plugin configuration service is the only owner of review selection.
+Use its existing user and workspace scopes; workspace values override the user
+default. Persist only a runtime-validated discriminated selection: inherit, or
+specified provider reference, model reference and optional supported reasoning
+level. An absent legacy option means inherit. No provider URL, protocol, API key
+or credential copy is stored in plugin options. No database migration is needed.
+The plugin settings expose follow-session / specified-model controls using the
+existing native model picker, reasoning options and provider-management screen.
+The provider screen owns custom Base URL, protocol and credentials. Saving must
+use the native plugins/configure command, survive restart and apply on the next
+review without changing the main session selection.
+
+The host reads effective configuration, validates its model reference against
+current native providers/models and supported reasoning/tool capabilities, then
+resolves the review model through native Chat Completions, Responses or Anthropic
+adapters. Deleted models, missing credentials, unsupported options/capabilities
+and malformed configuration yield specific technical failures and human approval.
+There is no fallback to a different provider or model.
+
+### Binding and lifetime
+
+Each approval snapshot binds the full action, real user authorization, session,
+turn, workspace identity/path, branch generation, main session selection, actual
+review selection and effective configuration version. The configuration version
+must reflect provider/model/credential changes as well as plugin options; values
+that may contain secrets stay host-only. Revalidate all fields before each model
+request, after it completes and before recording/executing a decision. A change
+invalidates the in-flight review immediately; its old result cannot authorize a
+new action. A permitted restart uses a fresh snapshot within the same three
+attempts and original 90-second deadline. Native calls use SingleAttempt.
+
+Runtime owns a private continuation map keyed by the active binding and review
+attempt. It preserves native assistant reasoning and provider metadata needed
+by that model's tool continuation. The host validates the visible transcript
+prefix before reconstructing subsequent native calls; the plugin cannot inject
+hidden state or receive it. Clear state on retry, stale binding, cancellation,
+disable, completion and lease close. Never share it with another review, the main
+model, plugin replies, progress, logs or delivery evidence. DeepSeek tool requests
+require complete previous reasoning_content, including assistant messages without
+tool calls: https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/thinking_mode/ .
+
+```mermaid
+sequenceDiagram
+  participant C as Native plugin/provider config
+  participant R as Session runtime (binding and continuation owner)
+  participant P as Approval plugin
+  participant M as Bound native model adapter
+  C-->>R: Effective selection and configuration version
+  R->>P: Bound action, authorization and visible context (bridge v2)
+  P->>R: Visible review transcript and read-only investigation schemas
+  R->>R: Validate snapshot and restore private continuation
+  R->>M: One attributed native stream
+  M-->>R: Visible output, tools, private reasoning and metadata
+  R->>R: Preserve private state for this binding only
+  R-->>P: Visible output and tools only
+  P-->>R: allow / deny / technical failure
+  R->>R: Revalidate, execute once or admit native human response
+  R->>R: Clear binding continuation
+```
+
+### Diagnostics and preserved policy
+
+Bridge v2 host and plugin ship together; a mismatched version fails to human
+approval. Progress and durable review records expose the actual review model.
+Failures may carry bounded business code, HTTP status, request id and retry
+information. All fields pass one sanitization boundary, excluding credentials,
+URLs with secrets, raw response bodies and stack traces. Explicit nonretryable
+provider interception stops immediately; technical failures do not increment
+policy denial counters. Preserve Codex policy, read-only investigation, native
+hard prohibits, Plan constraints, one-shot decisions, manual duplicate handling,
+truthful querySource=auto_review and the existing trace/session attribution.
+Do not bypass GLM interception by relabeling request identity.
+
+### Required acceptance and local delivery
+
+Test inherited/default and specified selection; custom providers; scope override;
+restart persistence; unchanged main model; missing/deleted/incompatible selection;
+allow executes once; deny executes zero times; 401, explicit service interception,
+broken stream, invalid output, timeout and cancellation; changing model/config or
+authorization during review; duplicate human responses; plugin disable. Force a
+read-only tool continuation and assert complete native hidden state, cross-review
+isolation and no state/credential leakage across the bridge or evidence.
+
+Run core, bridge and host regression on available Linux and Windows runtimes,
+isolated Windows UI regression, root and CLI typecheck/lint and architecture
+checks. Report baseline failures separately from new failures. Real Windows
+DeepSeek uses DEEPSEEK_API_KEY injected only into an isolated test host, official
+deepseek-flash with High reasoning. Clear temporary configuration on exit. Prove
+real automatic low-risk allow, controlled deny with a side-effect-free executor
+probe and file investigation. A missing key or transport restriction is an
+unverified scenario, never a success. Try GLM main session plus DeepSeek review;
+separately compare real same-account ordinary GLM and GLM review requests. Record
+their distinct outcomes; DeepSeek success does not prove GLM is unblocked.
+
+Deliver only locally under artifacts/0.1.3: independent Windows desktop, plugin
+ZIP, complete host patch, SHA256 checksums and sanitized acceptance report. Keep
+artifacts/0.1.2 intact for rollback. Update installation/configuration guidance
+and GLM status. No public publication, database migration or user-profile change.
